      "prefLabel": "Merge steward",
      "title": "Merge steward",
      "notation": "merge-steward",
      "description": "Stewards writes to ONE watched ref -- a long-lived branch several processes write and something downstream consumes serially. The ref is a parameter of the LANE INSTANCE, not of this persona, so `main`, `gh-pages` and each `cat/cat-harness/*` store branch can each have a steward without a schema change; a ref qualifies when a declaring directory's `storage` (or `source`) names it, or it is `main`/`gh-pages`. On `main` that work is a merge train: composes it from the queue, attributes and ejects on red, lands at the tested SHA. On a route-keyed ref it is coalescing: batches the writes arriving in one window into a single write. Decides nothing the reprioritisation table or the owner has not -- placement is computed by merge-priority.dmn, and landing waits for the owner's release. Records decisions on queue entries and windows, never the host's facts.",
      "sourceKind": "role-registry",
      "actorKinds": [
        "agent"
      ],
